A||||15||lennyb4||How do you guys (and ladies) do it???||||5||
Z||000000||lennyb4||06-08-2000||08:30 AM||||Ohhhh... Man i really need to get some more patience. My little baby need soooo much work (int. is roached, paint job is hazy, i could go on for an hour) but time and money has everything going soooo damn slow. I just want to get it done and show her off. Theres ALOT of side road car shows around my area and im dying take it. Drove past one last night and they were checking her out BUT with the condition shes in i dont want to show her to much (kinda like the ugly duckling) I know this is off subject but i had to get it off my chest before i pop!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phoenix||06-08-2000||12:43 PM||||Patients - man - patients - I've got one project car that been stripped down the the bare tub and acid cleaned and primed for 5 years now. A divorce, a 4 year old daughter and work keep me from it, but someday it will get done!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phoenix||06-08-2000||12:44 PM||||Patience - man - patience - I've got one project car that been stripped down the the bare tub and acid cleaned and primed for 5 years now. A divorce, a 4 year old daughter and work keep me from it, but someday it will get done!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fret Naught||06-08-2000||12:48 PM||||One day at a time, one piece at a time and one dollar at a time, remember, it is a hobby, if it isn't fun and relaxing, then maybe find something that is. It helps that my Fiero is not my primary transportation. So there is a lot less pressure.||||reg||7
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||06-08-2000||02:19 PM||||<BR>This post is not intended to flame, just trying to shoot the facts straight.<P>I can understand not wanting to show your Fiero until is pristine, but if everyone held back because it was less than perfect then we would not have any shows, except for the trailer queens.<P>Trailer queens are not cars, they are trophies.  Regardless of the amount of time, money, and effort they will never be driven. Yours is a driver, drive it and appreciate for it for being a Fiero, and be proud, you are a one of a few hundred thousand who own one.<P>Time and money will never be enough to do what you want to the car. You have a Fiero because you love it. You work on it because you love it. You drive it because you love it.<P>If we wanted a car with no headaches we would all be driving new cars.  Fieros come with maintenance, that is just the facts.<P>So as some might say "grin and bear it" but I say "I love it."  Working on and repairing your Fiero brings you closer to it, it is as close to love as you can get with an inanimate object.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||lennyb4||06-08-2000||02:28 PM||||GOLD86-SE... Thanks i needed that (a verbal slap around- kinda)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I do drive her everyday for now (putting her up this winter) and really do love to smoke the little pristine ricers around here. I guess i just get fed up and impatient now and then like im sure all of us have at one time or another. Drove her at lunch time and made me feel alot better.. And shes not as bad as i previously made her out to be. The worst part is the seats (look like they got into a fight with a cougar).<P>||||reg||6
Z||000006||dogtired||06-08-2000||02:59 PM||||Must agree with most above.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>A lot of the small clubs and shows have a category for work in progress? Sounds like you may be a contender??<BR>Patients is something that comes with age?? Lets see? the less time you have to live, because you are getting older, the more time you should wait?? Why do I have a problem with that? anyway!<BR>I don't think I would try and show it as work in progress for several years in a row at the same club?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Good Luck, Just hang in there.||||reg||6
Z||000007||batboy||06-08-2000||04:02 PM||||I feel your pain. I've sank much money and work into my Batmobile over this last year and it's still is another year from being to the point that I will be proud of it. Notice I didn't say before it's done, because projects are never completed (if you drive them). The poor Batmobile suffers from a crappy headliner, a boo boo on the hood, and a whole list of other things needing to be done, including a new paint job. However, I still love it.<P>The truck forum I belong to had a photo contest recently with different categories that included: restored, modified, daily drivers, incomplete projects, and "I just dragged it home & now I have to hide it from my wife" (my favorite).||||reg||1
Z||000008||Uaana||06-08-2000||07:31 PM||||I feel and share your pain brother.<BR>In the same spot. almost to the point where I'm willing to try to "Christine" it. IE sell my soul to the car and push it around the lot till it gets all better.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||06-08-2000||09:28 PM||||I think the main thing that helps is keeping your car clean. Vacuum out the trunk. Get some seatcovers. Take some rubbing compound to the paint. Most things can be fixed with a little money and a bunch of time. My car has a shredded drivers seat, chips in the clearcoat, faded paint, & cracked sail panels. I stil won a plaque for best modified fastback GT at our clubs show. It helped that there were only 2 cars in the class but thats part of it. Showing up is 50% of the battle. The other car in the class had new custom paint and body mods. My stuff was just cleaner than his.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||2M4 Dale||06-09-2000||12:53 AM||||I've had a bunch of really nice cars over the years !!! And I do mean a bunch. Seems to me that the day I feel as though this or that particular car is finished is also the very same day that it gets sold. So, this time, I've decided that my lowly 87 Econo-coupe will never be finished. When the day comes that I just can't seem to make something better I tend to lose interest. It's just like building a model. You get all intense over all the little details, etc. till it's finished then you put it on the shelf. Pretty soon it's covered with dust and then you let your kid play with it or something...lol||||reg||14
Z||000011||My7Fieros||06-09-2000||01:11 AM||||HERE HERE!! BRAVO!! WELL SAID GOLD86SE!!! Ive been getting real distressed about my formula...took it to my friends garage to finish prepping for paint, then to paint...now it wont even start!! I keep sinking more money into it, and trying to figure out why. It gets very dissapointing, to the point to where I just want to part it out and accept my $$ losses. But I know I can get it done.<BR>If you own a Fiero, you'll ALWAYS be putting $$ into it. These things will 10 dollar you to death. But thats just part of it I guess.<BR>When it is all said and done, you'll be very happy when you stand back and look at your work. Patience my friend. ;-)||||reg||14
Z||000012||Oreif||06-09-2000||01:23 AM||||Our local club (N.I.F.E.) has a car show every September. The "trailer queens" are only there for show! The "Daily Driver" cars are the ones that get the pizes and awards!<BR>Our club feels that they should honor the people who work on and drive every day. There even are prizes for "hard luck" cars.<BR>(although they state you cannot tow it in, it has to be driven!) Classes are divide by type (GT SE Coupe Formula) and then further broken down by year and Mileage! If you want to show off your Daily Driver make plans in September to visit! (there is even a prize for the car that was driven the farthest to get to the show!)<P>(Is this a plug or what!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-09-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000013||terryk||06-09-2000||12:34 PM||||Oreif,<P>I like that approach. It's the daily drivers that take the most work to maintain. I have a few friends with "trailer queens". The fact is, they bought the cars in that condition and haul them around to shows. Trophy Winner in a Can.......<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000014||wkayl||06-11-2000||01:25 AM||||I just got back Thursday from a 1,500 mile road trip in my GT to a car show where they had "work in progress" cars.  Mine was not one of them.  Some were dogs, but a few were realy works of art in the making.||||reg||1
